  "bookHagakureTitle": "Hagakure: The Book of the Samurai",
  "bookHagakureTag": "Discipline",
  "bookHagakureTheme": "Absolute discipline and resolve.",
  "bookHagakureWhyRead": "A radical text on the warrior's way (Bushido). It advocates for constant discipline and mental preparation against everything.",
  "bookHagakureKeyPhrase": "The Way of the Samurai is found in death (overcoming oneself).",
  "bookObstacleTitle": "The Obstacle is the Way",
  "bookObstacleTag": "Stoicism",
  "bookObstacleTheme": "Turning difficulty into advantage.",
  "bookObstacleWhyRead": "Learn to see problems not as walls, but as opportunities to grow and become better.",
  "bookObstacleKeyPhrase": "The obstacle is not meant to stop you, but to show you how much you want to move forward.",
  "bookEpicteteTitle": "The Enchiridion",
  "bookEpicteteTheme": "Radical Stoicism and Self-mastery.",
  "bookEpicteteWhyRead": "The absolute foundation. It teaches not to waste energy on what we cannot control and to focus solely on our effort.",
  "bookEpicteteKeyPhrase": "Some things are within our control, and some things are not.",
  "bookAureleTitle": "Meditations",
  "bookAureleTheme": "Mental strength and Inner dialogue.",
  "bookAureleWhyRead": "To show that an Alpha must be their own strictest judge. Ideal for staying the course during solitary training.",
  "bookAureleKeyPhrase": "The impediment to action advances action. What stands in the way becomes the way.",
  "bookSenequeTempsTitle": "On the Shortness of Life",
  "bookSenequeTempsTheme": "Time management and Philosophy of action.",
  "bookSenequeTempsWhyRead": "To eliminate the \"I don't have time\" excuse. This book motivates cutting out distractions to focus on what matters.",
  "bookSenequeTempsKeyPhrase": "It is not that we have a short time to live, but that we waste a lot of it.",
  "bookSenequeAmeTitle": "On the Tranquility of the Mind",
  "bookSenequeAmeTheme": "Serenity and Constancy.",
  "bookSenequeAmeWhyRead": "Learn to stay emotionally stable even when training is hard or results are delayed.",
  "bookSenequeAmeKeyPhrase": "We must get used to our condition, complain about it as little as possible, and seize all the advantages it can offer.",
  "bookBoeceTitle": "The Consolation of Philosophy",
  "bookBoeceTheme": "Resilience in the face of adversity.",
  "bookBoeceWhyRead": "Written in prison, this book is the ultimate lesson in mental strength: nothing and no one can take away your inner freedom.",
  "bookBoeceKeyPhrase": "Fortune has not taken everything from you, since you still have the use of your reason.",
  "bookAtomicTitle": "Atomic Habits",
  "bookAtomicTag": "Productivity",
  "bookAtomicTheme": "The power of small changes.",
  "bookAtomicWhyRead": "To understand that success is not a question of intensity, but of constancy and building viable systems.",
  "bookAtomicKeyPhrase": "You do not rise to the level of your goals, you fall to the level of your systems.",
  "bookLeBonTitle": "The Crowd: A Study of the Popular Mind",
  "bookLeBonTag": "Influence",
  "bookLeBonTheme": "Sociology and Group Psychology.",
  "bookLeBonWhyRead": "Essential to understand how to influence your surroundings and become a charismatic leader.",
  "bookLeBonKeyPhrase": "Pure and simple affirmation, free of all reasoning, is one of the surest ways of making an idea enter the minds of crowds.",
  "bookSchopenhauerTitle": "The Art of Being Right",
  "bookSchopenhauerTheme": "Rhetoric and Debate.",
  "bookSchopenhauerWhyRead": "To learn how to defend your vision and your Arc against skeptics. It is the intellectual armor of the Alpha.",
  "bookSchopenhauerKeyPhrase": "The truth is that every man wants to be right, by all possible means.",
  "bookLaBruyereTitle": "The Characters",
  "bookLaBruyereTheme": "Human Observation and Psychology.",
  "bookLaBruyereWhyRead": "To develop a piercing vision. Learn to read people like you read a running route.",
  "bookLaBruyereKeyPhrase": "Everything has been said, and we come too late after seven thousand years that there have been men who think.",
  "bookRochefoucauldTitle": "Maxims",
  "bookRochefoucauldTheme": "Human Nature and Realism.",
  "bookRochefoucauldWhyRead": "Short, punchy sentences (perfect for the app UI) that reveal the hidden springs of our actions.",
  "bookRochefoucauldKeyPhrase": "Our virtues are, most often, only vices in disguise.",
  "bookBalzacTitle": "Treatise on Elegant Living",
  "bookBalzacTheme": "Style, Energy and Social Presence.",
  "bookBalzacWhyRead": "For the user seeking aesthetic excellence and social radiance after forging their body.",
  "bookBalzacKeyPhrase": "Elegance is at once an art, a science, a taste, an enthusiasm.",
  "bookArtOfWarTitle": "The Art of War",
  "bookArtOfWarTag": "48 Laws of Power",
  "bookArtOfWarTheme": "Strategy and Emotional Mastery.",
  "bookArtOfWarWhyRead": "The bible of efficiency. Learn to conserve your strength to strike at the right moment.",
  "bookArtOfWarKeyPhrase": "The greatest conqueror is the one who knows how to win without a battle.",
  "bookMachiavelTitle": "The Prince",
  "bookMachiavelTheme": "Leadership and Realism of power.",
  "bookMachiavelWhyRead": "Understand group dynamics and hierarchy to lead your own Clan in Valerion.",
  "bookMachiavelKeyPhrase": "There is no other way to guard against flattery than to make men understand that telling the truth does not offend you.",
  "bookMusashiTitle": "The Book of Five Rings",
  "bookMusashiTag": "Strategy",
  "bookMusashiTheme": "Martial discipline and Total mastery.",
  "bookMusashiWhyRead": "The greatest samurai explains how to apply strategy in every small gesture. Perfect for technical Calisthenics.",
  "bookMusashiKeyPhrase": "From one thing, know ten thousand things.",
  "bookLaoTseuTitle": "Tao Te Ching",
  "bookLaoTseuTheme": "Balance, Fluidity and Harmony.",
  "bookLaoTseuWhyRead": "To counterbalance brute force. It is the book that helps reach the maximum Harmony Index.",
  "bookLaoTseuKeyPhrase": "Nothing in the world is more flexible and yielding than water. Yet, to attack what is hard and strong, nothing surpasses it.",
  "bookCastiglioneTitle": "The Book of the Courtier",
  "bookCastiglioneTheme": "Self-mastery and Sprezzatura (ease).",
  "bookCastiglioneWhyRead": "To cultivate that natural ease where the colossal effort behind the performance must never be seen.",
  "bookCastiglioneKeyPhrase": "Make appear effortless what was accomplished with great pain.",
